    "abstract": "The paper shows that state space models and variants of attention are closely related through structured semiseparable matrices, developing the state space duality (SSD) framework. SSD yields Mamba-2, whose core layer refines Mamba's selective SSM and is 2-8x faster while remaining competitive with Transformers on language modelling.",
    "domain": "NLP",
    "key_claims": [
      "An SSM with scalar-times-identity A is equivalent to masked linear attention with a 1-semiseparable mask L (state space duality).",
      "The SSD chunked algorithm computes the layer with matrix multiplications, combining quadratic intra-chunk and linear inter-chunk computation.",
      "The SSD core layer is 2-8x faster than Mamba's selective scan and allows much larger state sizes.",
      "Mamba-2 (parallel projections, extra normalisation, multi-head SSM) matches or beats Mamba and Transformer++ in LM scaling and improves on MQAR associative recall."
    ],
